# Files that must never be uploaded to a deployment.
#
# This matters most for drag-and-drop deploys: they upload the folder as it is
# on disk and do NOT apply .gitignore, so anything sitting here goes up.
#
# .data/ is the local development datastore. It contains the demo seed —
# fake clients, fake appointments, and a SUPER_ADMIN whose password is in the
# source. Uploaded, it makes a deployment *look* like it has a database:
# pages render, sign-in works, and every write silently fails because the
# filesystem is read-only. Real data belongs in Postgres via DATABASE_URL.
.data/

# Secrets, build output and dependencies — restored by the build itself.
.env
.env.*
.next/
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
